```

**Characteristics:**
- Uses static method pattern
- Stores formatted strings: `"[LEVEL] message"`
- No contextual data (user_id, ip_address, timestamp)
- Simple string concatenation
- Global static vector accumulates logs
- Typical of legacy CLI logging

#### New System (Structured Logging)

**File: `/src/logger/structured_logger.h` (lines 1-25)**
```cpp
#pragma once
#include <string>
#include <vector>

namespace logger {

struct StructuredLog {
    std::string level;
    std::string message;
    std::string user_id;
    std::string ip_address;
};

class StructuredLogger {
public:
    static StructuredLogger& instance();
    void log(const StructuredLog& entry);
    const std::vector<StructuredLog>& logs() const { return entries_; }

private:
    StructuredLogger() = default;
    std::vector<StructuredLog> entries_;
};

} // namespace logger
```

**File: `/src/logger/structured_logger.cpp` (lines 1-14)**
```cpp
#include "structured_logger.h"

namespace logger {

StructuredLogger& StructuredLogger::instance() {
    static StructuredLogger inst;
    return inst;
}

void StructuredLogger::log(const StructuredLog& entry) {
    entries_.push_back(entry);
}

} // namespace logger
```

**Characteristics:**
- Singleton pattern via `instance()` method
- Stores structured data via `StructuredLog` struct
- Fields: level, message, user_id, ip_address
- Machine-readable format (can parse field by field)
- Supports security auditing (tracks which user, from which IP)
- Facilitates JSON serialization, log aggregation, monitoring

